Z||000000||Blade||08-25-2000||12:17 PM||||I am gonna have a small crack int he front facia. whats the best way to repair this shor t of new facia as im not ready to do that fer a while.<P>Blade||||reg||1
Z||000001||deceler8||08-25-2000||02:25 PM||||Best way is to repair it from the rear with fiberglass cloth and resin. If you can do this, apply the cloth and resin to the rear, and hold the repair together while the part sits in the sun...this will cure the repair in a very short time.<P>If you do this well, the crack will be barely visible, and at worst, you might have to use some touch up paint on it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||rprevo||08-25-2000||03:32 PM|||| The proper stuff that is flexible enough<BR>for that plastic is SMC or just about<BR>any kind of plastic filler specific to<BR>saturns and fiero's I tried risin and<BR>it was to rigid for the soft plastic.<P>Ray<BR><P>------------------<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000003||wla21841||08-28-2000||06:03 PM||||The best thing to use is 3M 8101 body adhesive. You clean the area at least 1 1/2" arround the break. Apply the adhesive and fiberglass tape. The same way you would patch a drywall. Of corse from the back side.<P>The 8101 is available at most body paint supplies. I paid $14.27 for the kit.||||reg||3
